{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787361436504833001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"emulsible-beneficent-caiman","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":4,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"4ce2dc80debb4da6457e45df4df30e86839590f656b7b4ad2346117587b447b1","event_uuid":"99f1b402-60dc-4967-a353-c4b0099dcb4a","position":{"commit_sha":"6c35928791f7d89ba2891d0f6cca22ee84cb4e05","position":"1787358784667864001-99f1b402-60dc-4967-a353-c4b0099dcb4a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f75f64616d0e9f914bbaed2a39db8e5e79a6dbdd6abe05370711e1f424f8270e","event_uuid":"ee4ebfb1-f497-4d85-aee2-1e3c77082d2a","position":{"commit_sha":"eda5ae460a32eb62bbbec5e9e02775f2837cb47a","position":"1787358819450648001-ee4ebfb1-f497-4d85-aee2-1e3c77082d2a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"96a435a962e4f72a1e46dc42c6d44f6e834a6ed9aacc2e62524ba5be0121add8","event_uuid":"c4516fe9-5ec8-4c9e-8006-c03e518e3b36","position":{"commit_sha":"d444171e3e9ba90c53a73800fbebb5ebd5756ca8","position":"1787358839405856001-c4516fe9-5ec8-4c9e-8006-c03e518e3b36"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"225a243a75c1680464c2cb5561af226e4ddd1fb0f66c262854cb37aa966f9935","event_uuid":"031b9f84-7077-4a97-a177-60741aaf5cb2","position":{"commit_sha":"042b3f10344320113a276c2e6bebf29fd0fb02f3","position":"1787358879797588001-031b9f84-7077-4a97-a177-60741aaf5cb2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787358784667864001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"c4516fe9-5ec8-4c9e-8006-c03e518e3b36","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"9011-54d6-eb04-4cd6"},{"link_uuid":"031b9f84-7077-4a97-a177-60741aaf5cb2","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"dff2-9c38-c454-4daa"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py:42` escalates a bug fix to plan review only above 150 non-test lines. A backtest over 641 bug-fix commits on `origin/main` since 2026-06-15 (29 later introduced a bug; corpus from `scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --rev-range origin/main`) shows the floor catches 9 of 29. No signal computable from the diff beats it (file count, package spread, touched-function cyclomatic complexity, module fan-in, new-file: 3–12 of 29). The signal that does work is repeat fixing: a fix to a file that was bug-fixed at least twice in the prior 7 days catches 17 of 29 at 37% escalation; these are families fixed one instance at a time (`8d862d1058`, a 127-line fix, introduced five bugs). The rule is pure git history plus ticket type — no path lists — so it holds on any project and scales with that project's churn. Approved 2026-08-21.\n\n## Approach\nAdd a second escalation predicate beside the line floor in `bugfix_size_gate.py`: for each non-test file in the diff, count commits on the base branch in the prior 7 days that (a) touch the file and (b) carry a `rebar-ticket:` trailer or leading id resolving to a `bug` ticket (reuse `extract_ticket_refs` and the resolver the backtest already uses); escalate when any file's count is ≥ 2. Parameters `REPEAT_FIX_WINDOW_DAYS = 7` and `REPEAT_FIX_MIN_PRIOR = 2` sit beside `BUGFIX_SIZE_THRESHOLD_NON_TEST_LINES`. Mirror the predicate in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py:191-211` (`bug_blast_radius_escalates`) so `review-plan` on a bug runs the full rubric under the same condition. The teaching finding names the file and the prior fixes. Extend `scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py` to emit the repeat-fix flag so the rule stays backtestable with the gate's own code.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py`, `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py`, `scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py`, `docs/plan-review-gate.md` (escalation section), `tests/unit/llm/code_review/test_bugfix_size_gate.py`, `tests/unit/plan_review/test_bug_escalation.py`.\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: a fixture repo where a file has two prior bug-trailer commits inside 7 days escalates a 20-line fix; a file with one prior fix, or two fixes 8+ days old, does not. Edge: prior commits without a resolvable bug trailer do not count; merge commits do not count; the line floor still escalates independently. Pinning: existing `bugfix_size` tests and `--check-planning-corpus` pass unchanged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A bug fix touching a file with ≥2 bug-trailer commits in the prior 7 days is escalated on both the code-review gate and `review-plan`; checked by the new unit tests.\n- [ ] `python scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py --rev-range origin/main` reports the repeat-fix flag per commit and, over the 641-commit corpus, flags 17 of the 29 labelled commits; checked by running it and comparing to the corpus in this review's scratch data attached to the ticket.\n- [ ] The planning-corpus check still passes (`--check-planning-corpus` exit 0); checked by running it.\n","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/bugfix_size_gate.py","reason":"approved remediation edit"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/plan_review/orchestrator.py","reason":"approved remediation edit"},{"path":"scripts/backtest_bugfix_size.py","reason":"approved remediation edit"},{"path":"docs/plan-review-gate.md","reason":"approved remediation edit"},{"path":"tests/unit/llm/code_review/test_bugfix_size_gate.py","reason":"approved remediation edit"},{"path":"tests/unit/plan_review/test_bug_escalation.py","reason":"approved remediation edit"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["parent","2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a"],["relates_to","9011-54d6-eb04-4cd6"],["relates_to","dff2-9c38-c454-4daa"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["gates","fortnight-review"],"ticket_id":"1dd5-1880-17d0-4ac0","ticket_type":"story","title":"Escalate repeat fixes to plan review: a file bug-fixed twice in the prior 7 days","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["99f1b402-60dc-4967-a353-c4b0099dcb4a","ee4ebfb1-f497-4d85-aee2-1e3c77082d2a","c4516fe9-5ec8-4c9e-8006-c03e518e3b36","031b9f84-7077-4a97-a177-60741aaf5cb2"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787361436504833001,"uuid":"6a73383a-748d-4599-af8a-c9e2ea112076"}